"""Open SaaS starter kit manifest.

A 100% free, open-source SaaS boilerplate built on the Wasp full-stack
framework. Ships with auth, payments, background jobs, analytics, file
uploads, email sending, and an admin dashboard.

Architecture reference: https://docs.opensaas.sh/start/guided-tour/
Source: https://github.com/wasp-lang/open-saas
"""

from scryr import Diagram, Info, Link, Manifest, ManifestQuery
from scryr.types import (
    Classification,
    DeploymentTarget,
    IncrementalVersion,
    Markdown,
    MetricTool,
    ProgrammingLanguage,
    Url,
    WebFramework,
    parse_version,
)

_SOURCE = Url("https://github.com/wasp-lang/open-saas")
_DOCS = Url("https://docs.opensaas.sh/")
postgres_block = Manifest(
    name="PostgreSQL",
    icon="🐘",
    classification=Classification.database,
    tags=["database", "sql", "infra"],
    connections=[],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "## Application and job persistence\n"
            "\n"
            "Primary Prisma-managed PostgreSQL database. Stores all app data: users, sessions, subscriptions, daily stats, file records, and page view sources. Also hosts pg-boss job queue tables used by Wasp background jobs.\n"
            "\n"
            "> **Illustrative sample notes:** the checks below are design and runbook examples, not claims about an active deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Review focus |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Product records | Users, subscriptions, file metadata, and statistics |\n"
            "| Job state | Background work shares the relational database |\n"
            "\n"
            "### Walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Create a test user and enqueue a statistics job.\n"
            "2. Restore a test backup and verify both application records and job state.\n"
            "   - Capture the relevant request or job identifier.\n"
            "   - Compare the user-visible outcome with the persisted or provider state.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Failure handling\n"
            "\n"
            "**Watch for:** Heavy background processing can compete with interactive database queries.\n"
            "\n"
            "Suggested diagnostic signals: *connection pressure, slow queries, and oldest pending job*. Compare them over the same time window.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "observe the symptom\n"
            "  -> identify the affected dependency\n"
            "  -> reproduce with test data\n"
            "  -> verify recovery from the user perspective\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "### Readiness checklist\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Exercise the happy path with test data.\n"
            "- [ ] Rehearse the failure and recovery path.\n"
            "- [ ] Record the owner, evidence, and follow-up in the deployment runbook.\n"
            "\n"
            "~~Assume a green process means the workflow works~~ — verify the end-to-end outcome as well.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - SQL clients for read-only inspection\n"
            "  - Query plans for index review\n"
            "  - Migration tooling for schema changes\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "  - `jaeger`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("15.0.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.sql],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.railway],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.grafana,
            MetricTool.loki,
            MetricTool.jaeger,
        ],
        links=[Link(site_name="Open SaaS Docs", http_url=_DOCS)],
    ),
)
server_block = Manifest(
    name="Wasp Server",
    icon="⚙️",
    classification=Classification.internal_api,
    tags=["wasp", "server", "auth"],
    connections=[
        Manifest(name="PostgreSQL"),
        Manifest(name="Email"),
        Manifest(name="AWS S3"),
        Manifest(name="Stripe"),
    ],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "## Server operations\n"
            "\n"
            "Wasp-generated Node.js/Express backend. Handles all type-safe server operations (Queries &amp; Actions via RPC), multi-method auth (email + Google + GitHub + Discord), payment webhook processing (Stripe / Polar.sh / Lemon Squeezy), and pg-boss background jobs (e.g. hourly `dailyStatsJob` for analytics aggregation).\n"
            "\n"
            "> **Illustrative sample notes:** the checks below are design and runbook examples, not claims about an active deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Review focus |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Interactive requests | Authorize queries and actions using server-side identity |\n"
            "| Integrations | Coordinate billing, email, file metadata, and jobs |\n"
            "\n"
            "### Walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Run a protected operation with a test user.\n"
            "2. Repeat without authentication and verify that no private data is returned.\n"
            "   - Capture the relevant request or job identifier.\n"
            "   - Compare the user-visible outcome with the persisted or provider state.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Failure handling\n"
            "\n"
            "**Watch for:** A client-supplied user or subscription identifier must not decide authorization.\n"
            "\n"
            "Suggested diagnostic signals: *operation latency, dependency failures, and job completion delay*. Compare them over the same time window.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "observe the symptom\n"
            "  -> identify the affected dependency\n"
            "  -> reproduce with test data\n"
            "  -> verify recovery from the user perspective\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "### Readiness checklist\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Exercise the happy path with test data.\n"
            "- [ ] Rehearse the failure and recovery path.\n"
            "- [ ] Record the owner, evidence, and follow-up in the deployment runbook.\n"
            "\n"
            "~~Assume a green process means the workflow works~~ — verify the end-to-end outcome as well.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - `express`\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - TypeScript for static checks\n"
            "  - ESLint for source checks\n"
            "  - Playwright for browser workflows\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "  - `jaeger`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("0.22.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.typescript],
        frameworks=[WebFramework.express],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.railway],
        owners="Product",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.grafana,
            MetricTool.loki,
            MetricTool.jaeger,
        ],
        links=[
            Link(site_name="Wasp Docs", http_url=Url("https://wasp.sh/docs")),
            Link(site_name="Open SaaS Docs", http_url=_DOCS),
        ],
    ),
)
