stripe_block = Manifest(
    name="Stripe",
    icon="💳",
    classification=Classification.public_api,
    tags=["payments", "billing", "stripe"],
    connections=[],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "## Subscription lifecycle\n"
            "\n"
            "Stripe payment integration for subscription billing. The Wasp Server creates Checkout sessions and listens to Stripe webhook events (checkout.session.completed, customer.subscription.updated, etc.) to update user subscription tiers in PostgreSQL. Polar.sh and Lemon Squeezy are also supported as drop-in alternatives.\n"
            "\n"
            "> **Illustrative sample notes:** the checks below are design and runbook examples, not claims about an active deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Review focus |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Checkout | Start a hosted payment flow for the selected plan |\n"
            "| Reconciliation | Apply authenticated provider events to application subscription state |\n"
            "\n"
            "### Walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Complete checkout using provider test mode.\n"
            "2. Replay a test webhook and verify the same final subscription state.\n"
            "   - Capture the relevant request or job identifier.\n"
            "   - Compare the user-visible outcome with the persisted or provider state.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Failure handling\n"
            "\n"
            "**Watch for:** The browser return page is not proof that a payment event has been processed.\n"
            "\n"
            "Suggested diagnostic signals: *webhook failures, processing delay, and reconciliation discrepancies*. Compare them over the same time window.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "observe the symptom\n"
            "  -> identify the affected dependency\n"
            "  -> reproduce with test data\n"
            "  -> verify recovery from the user perspective\n"
