analytics_block = Manifest(
    name="Analytics",
    icon="📈",
    classification=Classification.public_api,
    tags=["analytics", "stats", "admin"],
    connections=[],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "## Product measurement\n"
            "\n"
            "Web analytics integration — either Plausible Analytics or Google Analytics. The Wasp Client sends pageview events; the Wasp Server's hourly `dailyStatsJob` pulls aggregated stats via the provider's API and stores them in PostgreSQL for display on the Admin Dashboard.\n"
            "\n"
            "> **Illustrative sample notes:** the checks below are design and runbook examples, not claims about an active deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Review focus |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Browser events | Collect the configured pageview signals |\n"
            "| Aggregates | Fetch provider summaries for the administrative view |\n"
            "\n"
            "### Walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Visit a test page and inspect its later aggregate entry.\n"
            "2. Delay a statistics job and confirm the dashboard exposes the reporting period.\n"
            "   - Capture the relevant request or job identifier.\n"
            "   - Compare the user-visible outcome with the persisted or provider state.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Failure handling\n"
            "\n"
            "**Watch for:** Provider totals and application totals can differ because of filters and timezones.\n"
            "\n"
            "Suggested diagnostic signals: *aggregation freshness, provider API failures, and missing reporting intervals*. Compare them over the same time window.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "observe the symptom\n"
            "  -> identify the affected dependency\n"
            "  -> reproduce with test data\n"
            "  -> verify recovery from the user perspective\n"
